WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
[TITLE MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.400
ANKIT MEHTA: GCP is a set
of solutions and products

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:15.270
that can help you solve your
toughest business challenges.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:19.050
We have external
paying customers

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:25.140
that run businesses on our
platforms and at massive scale.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:30.780
These customers expect
developer velocity and quality.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.820
MTHRA RAJAH: We have
thousands of engineers

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.320
at Google building this platform
at all levels of the stack.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.530
These engineers want a
seamless developer workflow,

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.230
deterministic signals,
insights, and velocity.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:47.850
ANKIT MEHTA: It is GCP
Engineering Productivity team's

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.560
role to balance these two
dimensions, between developer

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.670
velocity and quality.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:01.440
For example, we
deploy GCP's console

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:07.650
twice a week to our users,
and with high quality.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:13.260
Our goal is to establish
biweekly high-quality releases

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.820
across GCP.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.190
MTHRA RAJAH: At
Google, we have created

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:20.940
a set of guiding principles
that let us have both developer

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:23.250
velocity and quality.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:26.610
We want to share these
principles and the tools that

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:29.760
are available to you
so you can accelerate

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.120
at the pace your users expect.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.260
ANKIT MEHTA: While we
at Google initially

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:39.030
focused on test engineering,
over a decade ago,

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:41.310
we started looking at
engineering productivity

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.270
holistically.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:45.870
This gave us the
framework to achieve

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:50.912
the right balance between
developer velocity and quality.

00:01:50.912 --> 00:01:52.620
MTHRA RAJAH: This
meant that, in addition

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.010
to doing complex
qualification across systems,

00:01:56.010 --> 00:02:00.170
we started focusing on tooling
and infrastructure that enabled

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.720
developers themselves to
quantify their code changes

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.150
before they commit them.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.740
ANKIT MEHTA: This, in turn,
allows us not only to catch

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:14.220
bugs, but prevent them, too.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.850
This changed the way
we built, qualified,

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.760
and deployed our applications.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.600
And we started pushing the
boundaries of both developer

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:27.780
velocity and quality.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.760
MTHRA RAJAH: We balance
developer velocity and quality

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.580
at Google and on GCP
through Project Health pH.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.260
We track key metrics across
developer productivity,

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.800
release velocity, reliability,
and most importantly, quality.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:47.820
We automatically
calculate a pH level,

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:52.020
and aim to achieve a pH
level of 5 for all projects.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.640
ANKIT MEHTA: Our
guiding principles

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.260
are driving test health,
avoiding performance

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:03.630
regressions, and high-quality,
automated releases,

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:07.785
all of which are anchored
in actionable metrics.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.790
Let's zoom in on two of
these, driving test health

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:18.690
and avoiding
performance regressions.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:22.800
For driving test health, we
aim for hermetic integration

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:29.970
tests, fast [INAUDIBLE],, and
elimination of test flakiness.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:34.500
We have built a cloud
integration testing framework

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:40.680
internally that helps us
write test once, and run them

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.080
against any environment.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.700
MTHRA RAJAH: We
enable developers

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.730
to catch performance issues
early in the development

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.970
process to avoid
performance regressions.

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.490
We have a framework
that enables developers

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:56.940
to create sustainable
performance automation that

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.330
can gate releases on
performance criteria.

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:05.430
And we aim to improve GCP's
quality and deployment

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:09.440
by reducing manual toil,
increasing automation,

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.820
eliminating cherry-picks,
and improving

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.640
the fidelity of the test
signal in our pre-production

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.180
environments.

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.209
ANKIT MEHTA: Let's
dive deeper into what

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:22.230
we are doing for the
external developer and user.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:26.760
Google works closely with the
external Kubernetes and Istio

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:31.380
developer communities to
enable developer productivity

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:32.820
in open source.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:36.720
Kubernetes is an
open-source system

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.680
for automating deployment,
scaling, and management

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.820
of containerized
applications, while Istio

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:47.310
is an open-source
service mesh that

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:51.120
provides traffic management,
policy enforcement,

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:53.520
and telemetric collection.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:58.350
We are active contributors
to special interest group

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:01.212
SIG testing in Kubernetes.

00:05:01.212 --> 00:05:02.670
MTHRA RAJAH: Some
of the tooling we

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:06.740
helped build in the open
source community includes Prow,

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.860
the continuous integration
CI system used by Kubernetes

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.950
and a lot of other projects
that use Kubernetes.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.770
Prow is built on
top of Kubernetes.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:21.180
So our CI helps test
Kubernetes on Kubernetes.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:25.380
ANKIT MEHTA: Testgrid provides
a grid of test results,

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.860
making it easy to see
patterns over time,

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:34.320
provides fast access, and allows
interactive sorting, filtering,

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:37.100
grouping, and more.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:41.250
It is highly configurable, and
integrated with Cloud Build.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.100
MTHRA RAJAH: Recently, we
helped build hermetic testing

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.200
using Kubernetes and Docker.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:50.190
Kind brings up a confirmed
Kubernetes cluster locally

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.560
without any external
dependencies

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:55.890
for testing Kubernetes
changes or integration-testing

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:58.320
Kubernetes applications.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:01.140
Kubernetes was designed
with portability

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.020
and interoperability
in mind, and providers

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:07.110
want to enable
application portability.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.990
Google, alongside
other cloud providers,

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:13.020
helps out with the Cloud
Native Computing Foundation's

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:16.920
conformance program, which
ensures certified Kubernetes

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:20.490
products deliver
consistency and portability.

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:22.350
ANKIT MEHTA: The
outside world now

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:28.410
uses VNs, Kubernetes containers,
scalable storage, GitHub,

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:29.650
and so on.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:33.300
Google's software is stored
in a single shared repository.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:36.990
The development landscape
is rapidly changing,

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:40.790
and we are evolving our
tooling and incorporating

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:44.640
external tooling to adapt
to this changing landscape.

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:49.610
Summarizing, we believe that
if you prioritize driving test

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:54.120
health, treat performance
as a first-class citizen,

00:06:54.120 --> 00:07:00.360
and have automated CI/CD that
enables high-quality releases,

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:02.283
and measure everything--

00:07:02.283 --> 00:07:04.200
MTHRA RAJAH: --you can
have the same developer

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:07.080
velocity and quality as we do.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.730
[TITLE MUSIC PLAYING]

